# Terminates TLS for the API in production (PLAN-BACKEND.md §13) — on
# the VPS ops/Caddyfile is the one that runs; this local copy exists so
# the root stack boots standalone. With the `full` profile up it routes
# to the api service like the VPS does; without it, it answers alone.
#
# Container-internal ports stay standard (80/443); only the HOST side
# is overridden — docker-compose.yml maps 8081/8443 locally because
# 80/443 are commonly taken on dev machines. On the VPS the compose
# override maps 80/443 as usual.
:80 {
	reverse_proxy api:3000
}
